RDNA3-Hackintosh - third-party components and permissions

third_party/amd/        Verbatim or extracted headers from the Linux kernel
                        amdgpu driver (drivers/gpu/drm/amd, include/uapi/drm).
                        Copyright Advanced Micro Devices, Inc. and others,
                        MIT licence (text kept at the top of every file).

common/, kext/          Ports of logic from Linux amdgpu (MIT). Files that port
                        a specific amdgpu source name it in their header.

NullMoth NVIDIA driver  https://github.com/nullmoth/nvidia-macos-driver
                        (plugin/, kexts/: PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0,
                        translator/: LGPL-3.0-or-later, nvk/: MIT).
                        Its author granted this project permission, on the
                        NullMoth Discord (October 2026), to use the NullMoth
                        code in any way on the condition that it is used only
                        for AMD GPUs and does not interfere with NullMoth's own
                        NVIDIA work. Code derived from NullMoth in this
                        repository is used under that permission and must stay
                        AMD-only. A written confirmation from the author (e.g.
                        a comment in a GitHub issue of either repository) should
                        be linked here: TODO.
                        In this repository: accel/ (NullMoth accelerator),
                        fb/ (derived from NVRMFB), metal/ (plugin, translator).
                        The translator keeps its LGPL-3.0-or-later licence.

AMD firmware            Not included. See docs/FIRMWARE.md and LICENSE.amdgpu in
                        linux-firmware.
